===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[crowded]] manner; as [[completely]] or [[closely]] as possible.
#: {{ux|en|His study had books stacked '''chockablock''' on every shelf.}}
#: {{ux|en|The meeting hall was '''chockablock''' full of angry citizens.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=Oct 13, 2012|work=The Economist|url=http://www.economist.com/node/21564536|title=Free exchange: Concrete gains|passage=AMERICA is full of vast, empty spaces. Europe, by contrast, seems '''chock-a-block''' with humanity, its history shaped by a lack of continental elbowroom.}}

